;
; pjsip_trunks.conf.sample
;
; PJSIP transports for outbound trunks. The trunk endpoints / auths /
; aors / registrations themselves are provisioned at runtime via the
; realtime backend (see configs/samples/sorcery_realtime_agents.conf.sample),
; so this file only defines the transports they bind to.
;
; Generic: declare every transport the UI's transport dropdown can
; produce (udp/tcp). TLS lives in pjsip_transport_tls.conf so the
; cert path stays grouped with the rest of the TLS config.
;
; Appended into /etc/asterisk/pjsip.conf alongside the WSS transport
; from pjsip_wss_agents.conf.sample and the TLS transport from
; pjsip_transport_tls.conf.template.
;
; NOTE for editors: deploy/entrypoint.sh sed-injects
; external_media_address/external_signaling_address lines DIRECTLY
; under each [transport-*] header at boot. Never hand-add an
; external_media_address line here (it would defeat the injection's
; per-file idempotency check).
;
; ── DO NOT put deny=/permit= on a type=transport section ──────────────
; PJSIP transports have NO ACL options in this Asterisk version - an
; earlier revision of this file did exactly that (following stale
; chan_sip-era guidance that used to live in a comment here) and the
; result was NOT a rejected option but a rejected TRANSPORT: sorcery
; refuses to create the whole object ("Could not create an object of
; type 'transport' with id 'transport-udp'"), the UDP+TCP listeners
; never bind, and every trunk goes unreachable at once (confirmed live
; 2026-08-18: Voylo's health check went red the minute the image
; deployed). Scanner-flood filtering belongs in res_pjsip_acl (a
; [something] type=acl section in pjsip.conf, applies to all incoming
; SIP after transport, before endpoint lookup) or at the NLB security
; group - both still TODO; test either against a live carrier OPTIONS
; probe before trusting it.
;

[transport-udp]
type=transport
protocol=udp
bind=0.0.0.0:5060
; The NLB in front of this pod has NO UDP listener on 5060 - external
; SIP/UDP arrives on 5062 and is forwarded to 5060 (5060 itself is
; taken by the TCP listener; a single NLB port can't carry both
; protocols until the LB controller supports TCP_UDP listeners - see
; devops asterisk values.yaml). Without this override, the Contact
; header in our 200 OKs advertises :5060, so the carrier's in-dialog
; requests (the ACK for our 200 OK, the BYE when the caller hangs up)
; are silently dropped at the NLB. Missing ACK => Asterisk retransmits
; the 200 OK and tears the call down at 64*T1 = 32s ("inbound calls
; die at ~30s", confirmed live 2026-08-18 with duplicated 200 OKs in
; every inbound trace); missing BYE => the agent side never learns the
; caller hung up. Only meaningful once external_signaling_address is
; injected at boot (entrypoint.sh); harmless without it.
external_signaling_port=5062

[transport-tcp]
type=transport
protocol=tcp
bind=0.0.0.0:5060
; Carriers that only accept TCP (e.g. innocalls
; cu622.sip.innocalls.net:50760) use this transport; the source port
; the kernel picks for outbound is ephemeral, but binding here gives
; the transport a stable name that the realtime ps_endpoints.transport
; column can reference.
